# Consult Prosper docs before guessing

When a Prosper track rule, API field behavior, `reason` code, appointment
type, or problem's answer shape is unclear, follow
`docs/prosper-docs-navigation.md` ("When something is unclear, consult
before guessing"):

1. Read `docs/prosper-track-reference.md` first — it's the local snapshot,
   no network needed, and covers most of what's been gathered.
2. If that doesn't resolve it, or the detail is one that changes during the
   event (a problem's `open` status, its weight, the Scoring page's version
   string), fetch the live page directly. The docs site
   (`https://hackspain.getprosperapp.com/leaderboard/docs`) is a
   client-side JS SPA — a plain HTTP fetch returns nothing but the word
   "Prosper". Use whatever browser-rendering tool is available (an MCP
   browser/devtools tool if one is configured, or ask the person running
   this session to check the page) and navigate to the specific path from
   the page map in `docs/prosper-docs-navigation.md`.
3. If the live page disagrees with the snapshot, trust the live page and
   patch the specific fact into `docs/prosper-track-reference.md` so the
   next lookup is fast and correct.

Say which page confirmed the answer when reporting back. This rule mirrors
Claude Code's `consult-prosper-docs` skill in this repo — same procedure,
different harness.
